==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|haust}} from earlier {{m|non|haustr}} (masculine), from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*harƀustaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*harbistaz}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*kerp-}}. Compare Old English {{m|ang|hærfest}}, English {{m|en|harvest}}, the Old High German {{m|goh|Herbist}}; German {{m|de|Herbst}}, Danish {{m|da|høst}} and Swedish {{m|sv|höst}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/høyst/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|øyst|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|hausts|haust}}

# [[autumn]], [[fall]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég úrskrifaðist '''haustið''' 2007.|I graduated '''fall''' 2007.}}

